              "id": "CVE-2026-93748",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-93748: Use of Cache Containing Sensitive Information"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-93748?s=github&n=http-cache-semantics&t=npm&vr=%3C%3D4.2.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "http-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons.\n",
                "markdown": "> http-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons.\n\n|                                                                                                                                      |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:npm/http-cache-semantics@4.2.0  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <=4.2.0                             |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     not fixed                           |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                                      |\n"
